    "lecture-2-p007-london-currency": {
      "id": "lecture-2-p007-london-currency",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "lecture-2-p007-cross-market-quotes"
      },
      "reason": "The original image itself prints London price $100 and $100 times1.5300, while quoting USD per GBP. The arithmetic and intended arbitrage require a conditional £100 London interpretation; the inconsistent original dollar labels are preserved. This is not merely extraction corruption.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/lecture-2/page-007.md",
        "anchor": "lecture-2-p007-cross-market-quotes"
      }
    },
    "source-l3-p011-printed-rate-error": {
      "id": "source-l3-p011-printed-rate-error",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "lecture-3-p011-printed-continuous-solution"
      },
      "reason": "Original slide prints incorrect continuous and semiannual rates for growth 5800/5000 over 1.5 years. Printed equations/rates preserved; separately labelled correction awaits independent mathematical review.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/lecture-3/page-011.md",
        "anchor": "lecture-3-p011-labelled-correction"
      }
    },
    "source-l3-p016-rate-conventions": {
      "id": "source-l3-p016-rate-conventions",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "lecture-3-p016-printed-coupon-yield-table"
      },
      "reason": "Coupon versus yield par comparison requires matching compounding/payment conventions; source follows a continuously compounded yield example with a nominal semiannual coupon. Original table preserved; separate qualification awaits independent review.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/lecture-3/page-016.md",
        "anchor": "lecture-3-p016-rate-convention-caution"
      }
    },
    "seminar-2-problems-p002-annual-semiannual-conflict": {
      "id": "seminar-2-problems-p002-annual-semiannual-conflict",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "seminar-2-problems-p002-q7"
      },
      "reason": "Problem Q7 explicitly says annual coupon payments, while the supplied solution uses semiannual coupons and continuously compounded zero rates. Fractional-maturity annual coupon scheduling and zero-rate quotation are unspecified in the question.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/seminar-2-problems/page-002.md",
        "anchor": "seminar-2-problems-p002-q7"
      }
    },
    "seminar-2-solutions-p001-option-default-contradiction": {
      "id": "seminar-2-solutions-p001-option-default-contradiction",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "seminar-2-solutions-p001-q1-credit-risk"
      },
      "reason": "The same page acknowledges OTC option-writer default in Settlement but says option buyers face no default risk beyond premium in Credit risk. Preserve both and distinguish underlying-market loss from counterparty default.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/seminar-2-solutions/page-001.md",
        "anchor": "seminar-2-solutions-p001-q1-credit-risk"
      }
    },
    "seminar-2-solutions-p005-par-yield-average-qualification": {
      "id": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-par-yield-average-qualification",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-q6-par"
      },
      "reason": "The printed description of par yield as an average of spot rates weighted by cash flows is not a generally exact simple arithmetic-average rule; par yield is defined by the full discount-factor pricing equation.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/seminar-2-solutions/page-005.md",
        "anchor": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-q6-par"
      }
    },
    "seminar-2-solutions-p005-coupon-conflict": {
      "id": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-coupon-conflict",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-q7"
      },
      "reason": "The solution changes the question annual-coupon assumption to semiannual and explicitly chooses continuous zero rates. Treat its numerical answers as conditional, not uniquely implied by the question.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/seminar-2-solutions/page-005.md",
        "anchor": "seminar-2-solutions-p005-q7"
      }
    },
    "seminar-2-solutions-p006-rounding-equalities": {
      "id": "seminar-2-solutions-p006-rounding-equalities",
      "scopeRef": {
        "kind": "source",
        "unitId": "seminar-2-solutions-p006-q7-one-year"
      },
      "reason": "The source displays equalities involving rounded 0.0609 and 0.95718. They are approximations; use exact half-year discount factor 0.97 for verification.",
      "status": "open",
      "resolutionRef": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "path": "study/sources/annotated/seminar-2-solutions/page-006.md",
        "anchor": "seminar-2-solutions-p006-q7-one-year"
      }
    }
